  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Pass, return, accelerate and shoot",
  "description": "Half rink with a goalkeeper. The shooters queue up wide in the half, and a passer (B) stands to the right outside the penalty area. The drill has three steps.\n\n1. Stationary ball: place balls about one metre outside the penalty area. The shooter skates in and shoots the stationary ball. 2. Pass – return – accelerate – shoot: the shooter passes to B, accelerates and gets a pass back into their skating line, carries the ball a couple of strides and shoots. 3. The same, but now the shooter starts straight in front of goal and B stands to the left.\n\nThe shooter collects the ball and takes the passer's place; the passer joins the back of the queue. Switch sides after a while. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Accelerate straight after the pass – the shot should come at speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Take the ball on the first touch into your skating line, not stop-and-shoot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Look at the goal before you shoot and aim low and close to the post."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Passer: play the return in front of the shooter, not behind."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
